<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Network security configuration — cleartext HTTP for the local dev server.

    The <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true"> allows cleartext to ALL
    hosts. This is intentional for the MVP / academic demo where the server runs
    on the LAN without TLS. The user configures the server IP via Settings.

    PRODUCTION (A6 / S5): replace this with a domain-config that:
      1. Pins the production server domain.
      2. Sets cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" in base-config.
      3. Adds a domain-config for dev environments only (via a separate
         src/debug/ override of this file).

    Why not restrict to 10.0.2.2 only: the physical phone uses whatever LAN IP
    the user's PC has (e.g. 192.168.1.50). We cannot whitelist a fixed IP at
    build time without knowing it. The Settings screen + this permissive config
    is the correct pattern for a configurable LAN test tool.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
